Been playing around with illiterate cavepersons lately, just for a
laugh. It's great fun not having to worry about scrolls and spellbooks,
and a refreshing change from my usual wizards.

I]ve yet to get one even to minetown, and I've never got *anything*
more than a few levels into G, so ascension worries are largely
academic to me, but out of curiosity I looked uypa spoiler about how an
illitereate character tgets around the "book of the dead" thing.
Apparently you don't get around it at all- you just read the thing, and
the game doesn't count it as reading.

This strikes me as a bit of a cop out.

Therefore, I suggest an alternative: Allow another monster to read it
for you. I think that if you have the invocation artifacts, have
identified the VS, are standing near it, are in good favour with your
God and have maintained illiterate conduct so far, a prayer should
summon a co-aligned priest who will perform the ritual for you (once
you drop the artifacts and allow him to pick them up) and allow you to
proceed.

Of course, this screws up illiterate+atheist conduct, so i think any
intelligent pet should be able to do the ritual.

If you're attempting illiterate/atheist/petless, then you really are
beyond my help anyway=-)

It's quite a lot of work, I'll admit, for what seems like a very
superficial change, but this kind of thing really bugs me.



